-\subsection{Extensions that were not promoted}
+\section{Linear HPO Baseline Details}
 
-Several extensions were explored and intentionally not moved into the compact
-default.
+The linear cartesian-HPO baselines implement the complete preprocessing
+protocol requested for the comparison: 5 normalization choices, 10 smoothing
+choices, 3 baseline choices and 4 OSC choices, giving 600 preprocessing
+combinations.  PLS-HPO runs five Optuna trials per combination
+(3000 trial fits per dataset/seed), and Ridge-HPO runs ten trials per
+combination (6000 trial fits per dataset/seed).  The default-CV reference
+uses the same train/test splits without the cartesian preprocessing search.
 
-\begin{itemize}
-  \item The 100-operator default bank and the deep3/deep4 banks did not improve
-  the median external RMSEP enough to justify the added selection variance and
-  runtime.  Deep banks mostly reproduced the default-bank choice on the tested
-  splits.
-  \item OSC and EMSC branches were not promoted as defaults.  Existing
-  AOM\_v0 summaries show OSC variants hurting at the default
-  component setting and EMSC degree 1--2 being numerically unstable on small
-  splits.
-  \item SNV can help as a branch, but SNV+ASLS did not improve over ASLS alone
-  in the 57-dataset summary.  SNV, MSC, EMSC and ASLS remain branch
-  preprocessors, not strict fixed operators in the AOM algebra.
-  \item Fractional convolution kernel operators were implemented as diagnostic
-  bank extensions (\code{compact+FCK}: 9 compact operators plus eight FCK
-  kernels).  They remain useful evidence that fractional-derivative
-  preprocessors were considered, but they are not part of the current compact
-  recommendation until they pass the same paired, multi-seed and no-harm gates
-  as the compact AOM-PLS variants.
-\end{itemize}
+The successful complete HPO subset contains 36 PLS datasets and 35 Ridge
+datasets with three successful seeds.  The LUCAS\_SOC subset exceeded the
+available compute budget.  Two FUSARIUM response rows
+(\code{FinalScore\_grp70\_30\_scoreQ} and \code{Tleaf\_grp70\_30}) failed
+because the estimator input contained NaN values.  These rows are therefore
+excluded from HPO paired ratios but retained in the failure-mode ledger.
 
-\section{Benchmark Protocol Ledger}
+Against PLS-default, PLS-HPO has median ratio 0.993 on 36 datasets with
+21 wins.  Against Ridge-default, Ridge-HPO has median ratio 0.982 on 35
+datasets with 20 wins.  The HPO baselines are therefore strong but expensive:
+the observed successful-row totals are 162.4 h for PLS-HPO and 184.1 h for
+Ridge-HPO.
 
