+It is deliberately small.  Larger banks increase the number of candidates and
+therefore increase the risk of selecting validation noise.  With $B$
+operators and $K_{\max}$ component prefixes, a global selector considers
+approximately $BK_{\max}$ operator/component candidates before fold
+replication.  At $K_{\max}=15$, the compact bank has 135 candidates, whereas
+the 100-operator default bank has 1500.
 
-\subsection{Why fewer operators can be better}
+\begin{table}[h]
+\centering
