-\end{table}
+Let $B_j(\X)$ be a fold-local base representation such as raw spectra, SNV,
+MSC, EMSC or ASLS-transformed spectra.  For a chain $s$ and response vector
+$y$, the screening score used in FastAOM is
+\begin{equation}
+  \mathrm{score}(j,s)
+  =
+  \frac{\left\|A_s B_j(\X_c)\transpose y_c\right\|_2^2}
+       {\left\|B_j(\X_c)A_s\transpose\right\|_F^2
+        \left\|y_c\right\|_2^2}.
+  \label{eq:fastaom_screen}
+\end{equation}
+If $B_j(\X_c)\approx U_j\Sigma_jV_j\transpose$ is a truncated SVD and
+$F_{j,s}=A_sV_j\Sigma_j$, then the screened operator kernel is approximated as
+\begin{equation}
+  \K_{j,s}
+  =
+  B_j(\X_c)A_s\transpose A_s B_j(\X_c)\transpose
+  \approx U_j C_{j,s}U_j\transpose,
+  \qquad
+  C_{j,s}=F_{j,s}\transpose F_{j,s}.
+  \label{eq:fastaom_kernel}
+\end{equation}
+Kernel-vector products are therefore reduced to low-rank operations during
+screening.
 
-\section{Benchmark design and validation protocol}
+The four FastAOM model families are SingleChainPLSRidge, HardAOMChainPLSRidge,
+SoftAOMChainPLSRidge and SparseMultiKernelRidge.  The main results emphasize
+the two performant model classes: SparseMultiKernelRidge, which greedily
+selects chains in a sparse non-negative kernel mixture, and
+SingleChainPLSRidge, which fits PLS-Ridge on the top screened chain.  The hard
+and soft chain-routing strategies are part of the exploration reported in the
+supplement.
 
-\subsection{Datasets and splits}
+\section{Datasets and protocol}
 
-We used the local multi-dataset NIRS benchmark assembled in the repository.
-The benchmark contains heterogeneous regression and classification datasets
-covering a wide range of sample sizes, wavelength counts and response scales.
-The present paper focuses on regression because AOM-Ridge is currently a
-regression method and because the strongest AOM-PLS evidence is regression
-based.  Where an original train/test split existed, it was preserved.  When no
-external split was provided, deterministic SPXY or stratified variants were
-used \citep{kennard1969computer,galvao2005method}.  The external test set was
-kept untouched during preprocessing and hyperparameter selection.
+The cohort manifest contains 61 included local regression rows and 16 included
+classification rows.  The main AOM-PLS paired comparison uses 53 non-QUARTZ
+datasets with paired multi-seed AOM-PLS and PLS-standard rows.  FastAOM
+headline variants use 50--52 successful full-cohort datasets after filtering
+to variants with at least 50 completed rows.  The cartesian linear-HPO
+baselines use the complete successful subset: 36 PLS-HPO datasets and 35
+Ridge-HPO datasets with three successful seeds.  The LUCAS\_SOC subset
+exceeded the available compute budget in that cartesian campaign, and two
+FUSARIUM response rows failed estimator checks because the response contained
+NaN values.
 
