+Classification is a secondary validation axis.  The two performant
+AOM-PLS-DA variants are the SIMPLS classifiers: AOM-PLS-DA-global-SIMPLS
+improves balanced accuracy by a median 0.159 on 13 paired datasets with
+12 wins and $p=0.003$, and POP-PLS-DA-SIMPLS improves by 0.052 with 11 wins
+and $p=0.009$.  AOM-Ridge classification is also competitive: the global
+compact classifier gains 0.175 balanced accuracy on 14 datasets with 13 wins
+and $p=8.5\times10^{-4}$.  The supplement reports all AOM-Ridge
+classification variants, all of which are favourable in this cohort.
 
