-\subsection{Multi-seed regression robustness}
+The SIMPLS AOM-PLS-DA variants are the classification variants promoted in the
+main manuscript.  The NIPALS-adjoint classifiers are less stable: AOM-PLS-DA
+global NIPALS is positive but does not pass the Holm gate, and POP-PLS-DA
+NIPALS is negative at the median.  All five AOM-Ridge classification variants
+are favourable on the 14-dataset overlap, with median balanced-accuracy gains
+from 0.163 to 0.175 and 13--14 wins.  The global compact classifier is the
+single AOM-Ridge classification row used in the main text because it has the
+largest median gain.
 
