-\subsection{Parity validation}
+The failure ledger separates three categories.  The first category is
+denominator pathology, represented by QUARTZ in the manifest: absolute errors
+remain meaningful, but ratios are not used because the reference denominator
+is essentially zero.  The second category is estimator input failure, seen in
+the two FUSARIUM rows listed above; these rows contain NaN values for the
+linear HPO estimators.  The third category is ordinary model mismatch, where
+all models return finite predictions but the RMSEP spread is large.  Examples
+include Brix, Rice Amylose and LMA rows, where branch correction, derivative
+choice or default-bank operators can dominate the compact-bank selection.
 
